/-!
# The meridian of a knot and its preferred framing

Let `Φ : D² × S¹ → X` be a solid torus neighbourhood of a knot `f : S¹ → X` in a Hausdorff space
whose first and second integral homology vanish, such as `S³` or an integral homology sphere. The
boundary torus `T` of the exterior of the knot is framed by `Φ`
(`TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.framedBoundaryTorus`), with meridian `μ` and longitude `λ`.
This file computes the map `H₁(T; ℤ) → H₁(X ∖ K; ℤ)` induced by the inclusion of `T` into the knot
complement `X ∖ K`, `K` the image of `f`
(`TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.boundaryHomologyMap`).

* **The meridian generates `H₁(X ∖ K)`.** There is an isomorphism `H₁(X ∖ K; ℤ) ≃ ℤ` sending the
  class of the meridian to `1` (`TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.complementHomologyEquiv`). For
  a knot in `S³` this is the linking number with the knot, oriented so that the meridian of `Φ`
  has linking number `1`.
* **The framing number.** The longitude of `Φ` is homologous in `X ∖ K` to `n` times the meridian
  for a unique integer `n`, the framing number of `Φ`
  (`TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.framingNumber`); the class with `(μ, λ)`-coordinates
  `(p, q)` goes to `p + n q`.
* **The preferred framing.** Replacing the longitude by `λ - n · μ` gives the preferred framing
  `(μ, λ₀)` of the boundary torus
  (`TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.preferredFramedBoundaryTorus`). The preferred longitude `λ₀`
  is null-homologous in `X ∖ K`, and it generates the kernel of `H₁(T) → H₁(X ∖ K)`: in the
  preferred framing a class goes to its meridian coordinate. For a knot in `S³` this is the
  classical Seifert framing, whose longitude bounds a Seifert surface (Seifert surfaces are not
  formalized here); the `0`-framing of surgery theory and the `ℚ ∪ {∞}` surgery coefficients
  refer to it.

The homology hypotheses are stated for reduced singular homology in degrees `1` and `2`. For the
unit sphere of a four-dimensional real inner product space they are
`TauCeti.isZero_reducedSingularHomologyFunctor_sphere_of_ne`, and a `C²` knot in it has solid torus
neighbourhoods by `TauCeti.exists_isSolidTorusNeighborhood_sphere`.

The computation is the Mayer–Vietoris sequence of the cover of `X` by the open solid torus
`U = Φ (B² × S¹)` and the knot complement `X ∖ K`. Their intersection is the punctured open solid
torus `Φ ((B² ∖ {0}) × S¹)`, which is homotopy equivalent to the torus `S¹ × S¹` at radius
`1 / 2`. Since `H₂(X)` and `H₁(X)` vanish, `H₁(U ∩ (X ∖ K)) ≅ H₁(U) ⊕ H₁(X ∖ K)`. The meridian
dies in `U`, while the longitude survives in `U`, since it maps to a generator of `H₁(S¹)` under
the projection of `U` to its core. Hence `H₁(X ∖ K)` is freely generated by the meridian at
radius `1 / 2`, which is homotopic in `X ∖ K` to the meridian on the boundary torus.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.boundaryHomologyMap`: the map `H₁(T) → H₁(X ∖ K)`.
* `TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.complementHomologyEquiv`: the isomorphism `H₁(X ∖ K) ≃ ℤ`
  sending the meridian to `1`.
* `TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.framingNumber`: the framing number of `Φ`.
* `TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.preferredFramedBoundaryTorus`: the preferred framing of the
  boundary torus.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.complementHomologyEquiv_boundaryHomologyMap`: a class with
  `(μ, λ)`-coordinates `(p, q)` goes to `p + n q`.
* `TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.complementHomologyEquiv_boundaryHomologyMap_preferred`: a
  class goes to its meridian coordinate in the preferred framing.
* `TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.boundaryHomologyMap_preferredFramedBoundaryTorus_basis_one`:
  the preferred longitude is null-homologous in the knot complement.
* `TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.ker_boundaryHomologyMap`: the preferred longitude generates the
  kernel of `H₁(T) → H₁(X ∖ K)`.

## References

* D. Rolfsen, *Knots and Links*, Publish or Perish (1976), Section 2E: meridians and longitudes of
  a solid torus, and Exercise 2E7 and Definition 2E8, the preferred framing of a solid torus in
  `S³`, whose longitude is the unique one homologically trivial in the exterior.
* A. Hatcher, *Algebraic Topology*, Section 2.2, the Mayer–Vietoris sequence.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Limits Set Metric Function Topology TauCeti.HurewiczOne

namespace TauCeti

/-! ### First homology of the torus `S¹ × S¹` -/

/-- The map induced on first integral singular homology by a continuous map. -/
private abbrev H1map {Y Z : Type} [TopologicalSpace Y] [TopologicalSpace Z] (g : C(Y, Z)) :
    ((singularChains ℤ).obj (TopCat.of Y)).homology 1 →ₗ[ℤ]
      ((singularChains ℤ).obj (TopCat.of Z)).homology 1 :=
  (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ((singularChains ℤ).map (TopCat.ofHom g)) 1).hom

private theorem H1map_comp {Y Z W : Type} [TopologicalSpace Y] [TopologicalSpace Z]
    [TopologicalSpace W] (g : C(Z, W)) (g' : C(Y, Z)) (x) :
    H1map (g.comp g') x = H1map g (H1map g' x) := by
  rw [H1map, TopCat.ofHom_comp, Functor.map_comp, HomologicalComplex.homologyMap_comp,
    ModuleCat.hom_comp, LinearMap.comp_apply]

private theorem H1map_eq_of_homotopic {Y Z : Type} [TopologicalSpace Y] [TopologicalSpace Z]
    {g g' : C(Y, Z)} (H : g.Homotopic g') : H1map g = H1map g' :=
  congrArg ModuleCat.Hom.hom
    (TopCat.Homotopy.congr_homologyMap_singularChainComplexFunctor
      (f := TopCat.ofHom g) (g := TopCat.ofHom g') H.some (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) 1)

/-- A homotopy equivalence induces a bijection on first homology. -/
private theorem bijective_H1map {Y Z : Type} [TopologicalSpace Y] [TopologicalSpace Z]
    (e : ContinuousMap.HomotopyEquiv Y Z) : Bijective (H1map e.toFun) := by
  have :=
    ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (e.reducedSingularHomologyIso (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) 1).hom
  rwa [ContinuousMap.HomotopyEquiv.reducedSingularHomologyIso_hom,
    reducedSingularHomologyFunctor_succ] at this

/-- The class of the `(p, q)` curve of `S¹ × S¹`. -/
private abbrev torusClass (p q : ℤ) :
    ((singularChains ℤ).obj (TopCat.of (Circle × Circle))).homology 1 :=
  H₁AddEquivHomology (TopCat.of (Circle × Circle)) (loopClass (torusCurve p q))

private theorem H1map_torusClass {Y : Type} [TopologicalSpace Y] (g : C(Circle × Circle, Y))
    (p q : ℤ) :
    H1map g (torusClass p q) =
      H₁AddEquivHomology (TopCat.of Y) (loopClass ((torusCurve p q).map g.continuous)) :=
  homologyMap_H₁AddEquivHomology_loopClass (TopCat.ofHom g) _

private theorem circleProdFirstHomologyEquiv_torusClass (p q : ℤ) :
    circleProdFirstHomologyEquiv (Homeomorph.refl (Circle × Circle)) (torusClass p q) = ![p, q] :=
  circleProdFirstHomologyEquiv_torusCurve (Homeomorph.refl _) p q

private theorem torusClass_eq (p q : ℤ) :
    torusClass p q = p • torusClass 1 0 + q • torusClass 0 1 := by
  apply (circleProdFirstHomologyEquiv (Homeomorph.refl (Circle × Circle))).injective
  rw [map_add, map_zsmul, map_zsmul, circleProdFirstHomologyEquiv_torusClass,
    circleProdFirstHomologyEquiv_torusClass, circleProdFirstHomologyEquiv_torusClass]
  ext i
  fin_cases i <;> simp

private theorem exists_eq_torusClass
    (x : ((singularChains ℤ).obj (TopCat.of (Circle × Circle))).homology 1) :
    ∃ p q : ℤ, x = torusClass p q := by
  refine ⟨circleProdFirstHomologyEquiv (Homeomorph.refl _) x 0,
    circleProdFirstHomologyEquiv (Homeomorph.refl _) x 1, ?_⟩
  apply (circleProdFirstHomologyEquiv (Homeomorph.refl (Circle × Circle))).injective
  rw [circleProdFirstHomologyEquiv_torusClass]
  ext i
  fin_cases i <;> rfl

private theorem torusClass_eq_zero_iff (p q : ℤ) : torusClass p q = 0 ↔ p = 0 ∧ q = 0 := by
  rw [← (circleProdFirstHomologyEquiv (Homeomorph.refl (Circle × Circle))).map_eq_zero_iff,
    circleProdFirstHomologyEquiv_torusClass]
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ⟨congrFun h 0, congrFun h 1⟩, ?_⟩
  rintro ⟨rfl, rfl⟩
  ext i
  fin_cases i <;> rfl

/-! ### Mayer–Vietoris in degree one -/

/-- For an open cover `X = U ∪ V` of a space with `H₁(X) = H₂(X) = 0`, the Mayer–Vietoris map
`H₁(U ∩ V) → H₁(U) ⊕ H₁(V)` is bijective. -/
private theorem mayerVietoris_one {X : Type} [TopologicalSpace X] {U V : Set X} (hU : IsOpen U)
    (hV : IsOpen V) (hUV : U ∪ V = univ)
    (h₁ : IsZero ((reducedSingularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) 1).obj (TopCat.of X)))
    (h₂ : IsZero ((reducedSingularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) 2).obj (TopCat.of X))) :
    (∀ x, H1map (ContinuousMap.inclusion (inter_subset_left (t := V))) x = 0 →
      H1map (ContinuousMap.inclusion (inter_subset_right (s := U))) x = 0 → x = 0) ∧
    ∀ c, ∃ x, H1map (ContinuousMap.inclusion (inter_subset_left (t := V))) x = 0 ∧
      H1map (ContinuousMap.inclusion (inter_subset_right (s := U))) x = c := by
  rw [reducedSingularHomologyFunctor_succ] at h₁ h₂
  have hiso := TopCat.isIso_mayerVietorisToBiprod_of_isZero (X := TopCat.of X)
    (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) hU hV hUV 1 h₂ h₁
  set M := SSet.mayerVietorisToBiprod (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ)
      (TopCat.toSSet.map (TopCat.ofHom (ContinuousMap.inclusion (inter_subset_left (t := V)))))
      (TopCat.toSSet.map (TopCat.ofHom (ContinuousMap.inclusion (inter_subset_right (s := U))))) 1
  -- Read the biproduct `H₁(U) ⊞ H₁(V)` as the product module, where elements have coordinates.
  set P := M ≫ (ModuleCat.biprodIsoProd _ _).hom
  have hP : Bijective P.hom := ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso P
  have hfst : ∀ x, (P.hom x).1 =
      H1map (ContinuousMap.inclusion (inter_subset_left (t := V))) x := fun x ↦ by
    have hc : P ≫ (ModuleCat.biprodIsoProd _ _).inv ≫ biprod.fst = SSet.homologyMap
        (TopCat.toSSet.map (TopCat.ofHom (ContinuousMap.inclusion (inter_subset_left (t := V)))))
        (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) 1 := by
      simp only [P, M, Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc, SSet.mayerVietorisToBiprod_fst]
    rw [ModuleCat.biprodIsoProd_inv_comp_fst] at hc
    exact congr($(hc).hom x)
  have hsnd : ∀ x, (P.hom x).2 =
      -H1map (ContinuousMap.inclusion (inter_subset_right (s := U))) x := fun x ↦ by
    have hc : P ≫ (ModuleCat.biprodIsoProd _ _).inv ≫ biprod.snd = -SSet.homologyMap
        (TopCat.toSSet.map (TopCat.ofHom (ContinuousMap.inclusion (inter_subset_right (s := U)))))
        (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) 1 := by
      simp only [P, M, Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc, SSet.mayerVietorisToBiprod_snd]
    rw [ModuleCat.biprodIsoProd_inv_comp_snd] at hc
    exact congr($(hc).hom x)
  refine ⟨fun x hx hx' ↦ ?_, fun c ↦ ?_⟩
  · have h0 : P.hom x = 0 :=
      Prod.ext ((hfst x).trans hx) ((hsnd x).trans (by rw [hx', neg_zero]; rfl))
    exact hP.1 (h0.trans (map_zero P.hom).symm)
  · obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hP.2 (0, -c)
    exact ⟨x, (hfst x).symm.trans (congrArg Prod.fst hx),
      neg_injective ((hsnd x).symm.trans (congrArg Prod.snd hx))⟩

namespace IsSolidTorusNeighborhood

variable {X : Type} [TopologicalSpace X] {f : Circle → X} {Φ : SolidTorus → X}

/-! ### The open and the punctured open solid torus -/

/-- The open solid torus `B² × S¹`, mapped by `Φ`. -/
private def openSolidTorusMap (Φ : SolidTorus → X) (x : ↥(ball (0 : ℂ) 1) × Circle) : X :=
  Φ (⟨x.1, ball_subset_closedBall x.1.2⟩, x.2)

omit [TopologicalSpace X] in
private theorem range_openSolidTorusMap :
    range (openSolidTorusMap Φ) = Φ '' {p | ‖(p.1 : ℂ)‖ < 1} := by
  ext x
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨y, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨_, mem_ball_zero_iff.mp y.1.2, rfl⟩
  · rintro ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨(⟨p.1, by simpa using hp⟩, p.2), rfl⟩

/-- The punctured open solid torus `(B² ∖ {0}) × S¹`, mapped by `Φ`. -/
private def puncturedMap (Φ : SolidTorus → X) (x : ↥(ball (0 : ℂ) 1 \ {0}) × Circle) : X :=
  Φ (⟨x.1, ball_subset_closedBall x.1.2.1⟩, x.2)

private theorem range_puncturedMap (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    range (puncturedMap Φ) = Φ '' {p | ‖(p.1 : ℂ)‖ < 1} ∩ (range f)ᶜ := by
  ext x
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨y, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨⟨_, mem_ball_zero_iff.mp y.1.2.1, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
    rw [mem_compl_iff, puncturedMap, h.apply_mem_range_iff]
    exact y.1.2.2
  · rintro ⟨⟨p, hp, rfl⟩, hpf⟩
    rw [mem_compl_iff, h.apply_mem_range_iff] at hpf
    exact ⟨(⟨p.1, by simpa using hp, hpf⟩, p.2), rfl⟩

/-- `Φ` identifies `B² × S¹` with the open solid torus. -/
private def openSolidTorusHomeomorph (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    (↥(ball (0 : ℂ) 1) × Circle) ≃ₜ ↥(Φ '' {p | ‖(p.1 : ℂ)‖ < 1}) :=
  (h.isEmbedding.comp ((IsEmbedding.inclusion ball_subset_closedBall).prodMap
    IsEmbedding.id)).toHomeomorph.trans (Homeomorph.setCongr range_openSolidTorusMap)

private theorem coe_openSolidTorusHomeomorph_apply (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) (x) :
    (h.openSolidTorusHomeomorph x : X) = openSolidTorusMap Φ x :=
  (rfl)

/-- `Φ` identifies `(B² ∖ {0}) × S¹` with the open solid torus minus the knot. -/
private def puncturedHomeomorph (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    (↥(ball (0 : ℂ) 1 \ {0}) × Circle) ≃ₜ ↥(Φ '' {p | ‖(p.1 : ℂ)‖ < 1} ∩ (range f)ᶜ) :=
  (h.isEmbedding.comp ((IsEmbedding.inclusion (sdiff_subset.trans ball_subset_closedBall)).prodMap
    IsEmbedding.id)).toHomeomorph.trans (Homeomorph.setCongr h.range_puncturedMap)

private theorem coe_puncturedHomeomorph_apply (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) (x) :
    (h.puncturedHomeomorph x : X) = puncturedMap Φ x :=
  (rfl)

/-- The point `(r u, z)` of the solid torus, for `0 ≤ r ≤ 1` and `(u, z) ∈ S¹ × S¹`. -/
private def radialPoint (r : ℝ) (hr : r ∈ Icc (0 : ℝ) 1) (q : Circle × Circle) : SolidTorus :=
  (⟨(r : ℂ) * q.1, mem_closedBall_zero_iff.2 (by simpa [abs_of_nonneg hr.1] using hr.2)⟩, q.2)

private theorem continuous_radialPoint {Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace Y] {r : Y → ℝ}
    (hr : Continuous r) (hr' : ∀ y, r y ∈ Icc (0 : ℝ) 1) {q : Y → Circle × Circle}
    (hq : Continuous q) : Continuous fun y ↦ radialPoint (r y) (hr' y) (q y) :=
  (Continuous.subtype_mk (by fun_prop) _).prodMk (by fun_prop)

private theorem radialPoint_congr {r r' : ℝ} (hrr' : r = r') (hr : r ∈ Icc (0 : ℝ) 1)
    (hr' : r' ∈ Icc (0 : ℝ) 1) (q : Circle × Circle) :
    radialPoint r hr q = radialPoint r' hr' q := by
  subst hrr'
  rfl

private theorem radialPoint_zero (q : Circle × Circle) (hr : (0 : ℝ) ∈ Icc (0 : ℝ) 1) :
    radialPoint 0 hr q = (0, q.2) :=
  Prod.ext (Subtype.ext (by simp [radialPoint])) rfl

private theorem radialPoint_one (q : Circle × Circle) (hr : (1 : ℝ) ∈ Icc (0 : ℝ) 1) :
    radialPoint 1 hr q = SolidTorus.boundaryInclusion q :=
  Prod.ext (Subtype.ext (by simp [radialPoint])) (SolidTorus.boundaryInclusion_snd q).symm

private theorem norm_radialPoint (r : ℝ) (hr : r ∈ Icc (0 : ℝ) 1) (q : Circle × Circle) :
    ‖((radialPoint r hr q).1 : ℂ)‖ = r := by
  simp [radialPoint, abs_of_nonneg hr.1]

private theorem apply_radialPoint_notMem_range (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) {r : ℝ}
    (hr0 : 0 < r) (hr : r ∈ Icc (0 : ℝ) 1) (q : Circle × Circle) :
    Φ (radialPoint r hr q) ∉ range f := by
  rw [h.apply_mem_range_iff, ← norm_eq_zero, norm_radialPoint]
  exact hr0.ne'

/-- The torus at radius `1 / 2` is a deformation retract of the punctured open solid torus: the
homotopy equivalence `S¹ × S¹ ≃ₕ U ∖ K`, `(u, z) ↦ Φ (u / 2, z)`. -/
private def torusHomotopyEquiv (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    ContinuousMap.HomotopyEquiv (Circle × Circle) ↥(Φ '' {p | ‖(p.1 : ℂ)‖ < 1} ∩ (range f)ᶜ) :=
  (((sphereCircleHomeomorph (0 : ℂ) one_half_pos).symm.prodCongr
      (Homeomorph.refl Circle)).toHomotopyEquiv.trans
    ((((convex_ball (0 : ℂ) 1).starConvex (mem_ball_self one_pos)).sphereHomotopyEquiv
      one_half_pos (sphere_subset_ball one_half_lt_one)).prodCongr
        (ContinuousMap.HomotopyEquiv.refl Circle))).trans
    h.puncturedHomeomorph.toHomotopyEquiv

private theorem coe_torusHomotopyEquiv_apply (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ)
    (q : Circle × Circle) :
    (h.torusHomotopyEquiv q : X) = Φ (radialPoint (1 / 2) ⟨by norm_num, by norm_num⟩ q) := by
  simp only [torusHomotopyEquiv, ContinuousMap.HomotopyEquiv.trans_apply,
    Homeomorph.coe_toHomotopyEquiv, coe_puncturedHomeomorph_apply, puncturedMap]
  refine congrArg Φ (Prod.ext (Subtype.ext ?_) rfl)
  simp [ContinuousMap.HomotopyEquiv.prodCongr, radialPoint]

/-- The inclusion of the punctured open solid torus in the open solid torus. -/
private abbrev puncturedToOpen (f : Circle → X) (Φ : SolidTorus → X) :
    C(↥(Φ '' {p | ‖(p.1 : ℂ)‖ < 1} ∩ (range f)ᶜ), ↥(Φ '' {p | ‖(p.1 : ℂ)‖ < 1})) :=
  ContinuousMap.inclusion inter_subset_left

/-- The inclusion of the punctured open solid torus in the knot complement. -/
private abbrev puncturedToComplement (f : Circle → X) (Φ : SolidTorus → X) :
    C(↥(Φ '' {p | ‖(p.1 : ℂ)‖ < 1} ∩ (range f)ᶜ), ↥(range f)ᶜ) :=
  ContinuousMap.inclusion inter_subset_right

/-- The core map `S¹ × S¹ → U`, `(u, z) ↦ Φ (0, z)`. -/
private def coreMap (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    C(Circle × Circle, ↥(Φ '' {p | ‖(p.1 : ℂ)‖ < 1})) :=
  ⟨fun q ↦ ⟨Φ (0, q.2), _, by simp, rfl⟩,
    (h.isEmbedding.continuous.comp (continuous_const.prodMk continuous_snd)).subtype_mk _⟩

/-- The radial contraction of the torus at radius `1 / 2` onto the core, inside the open solid
torus. -/
private def contractHomotopy (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    ((puncturedToOpen f Φ).comp h.torusHomotopyEquiv.toFun).Homotopy h.coreMap where
  toFun x := ⟨Φ (radialPoint ((1 - x.1) / 2)
      ⟨by linarith [unitInterval.le_one x.1], by linarith [unitInterval.nonneg x.1]⟩ x.2),
    _, (norm_radialPoint _ _ _).trans_lt (by linarith [unitInterval.nonneg x.1]), rfl⟩
  continuous_toFun := (h.isEmbedding.continuous.comp (continuous_radialPoint (by fun_prop) _
    continuous_snd)).subtype_mk _
  map_zero_left q := Subtype.ext <| by
    simp only [ContinuousMap.comp_apply, ContinuousMap.inclusion_apply_coe,
      coe_torusHomotopyEquiv_apply]
    exact congrArg Φ (radialPoint_congr (by simp) _ _ q)
  map_one_left q := Subtype.ext <| by
    simp only [coreMap, ContinuousMap.coe_mk]
    exact congrArg Φ ((radialPoint_congr (by simp) _ ⟨le_rfl, zero_le_one⟩ q).trans
      (radialPoint_zero q _))

/-- The projection of the open solid torus to its core, followed by `z ↦ (1, z)`. -/
private def openToTorus (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    C(↥(Φ '' {p | ‖(p.1 : ℂ)‖ < 1}), Circle × Circle) :=
  ⟨fun y ↦ (1, (h.openSolidTorusHomeomorph.symm y).2), by fun_prop⟩

private theorem openToTorus_puncturedToOpen (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ)
    (q : Circle × Circle) :
    h.openToTorus (puncturedToOpen f Φ (h.torusHomotopyEquiv q)) = (1, q.2) := by
  have : h.openSolidTorusHomeomorph.symm (puncturedToOpen f Φ (h.torusHomotopyEquiv q)) =
      (⟨(2⁻¹ : ℂ) * q.1, by simp; norm_num⟩, q.2) := by
    rw [Homeomorph.symm_apply_eq]
    apply Subtype.ext
    rw [coe_openSolidTorusHomeomorph_apply]
    simp only [ContinuousMap.inclusion_apply_coe, coe_torusHomotopyEquiv_apply,
      openSolidTorusMap]
    exact congrArg Φ (Prod.ext (Subtype.ext (by simp [radialPoint])) rfl)
  simp [openToTorus, this]

/-- The meridian at radius `1 / 2` dies in the open solid torus. -/
private theorem H1map_puncturedToOpen_torusClass_zero (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ)
    (p : ℤ) :
    H1map (puncturedToOpen f Φ) (H1map h.torusHomotopyEquiv.toFun (torusClass p 0)) = 0 := by
  rw [← H1map_comp, H1map_eq_of_homotopic ⟨h.contractHomotopy⟩, H1map_torusClass,
    loopClass_eq_of_apply_eq _ (Path.refl (h.coreMap (1, 1))) fun t ↦ Subtype.ext (by
      rw [Path.map_coe, comp_apply, Path.refl_apply, torusCurve_apply]
      simp [coreMap]),
    loopClass_refl, map_zero]

/-- A class at radius `1 / 2` with a nonzero longitude coordinate survives in the open solid
torus. -/
private theorem eq_zero_of_H1map_puncturedToOpen_eq_zero (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ)
    {p q : ℤ}
    (hpq : H1map (puncturedToOpen f Φ) (H1map h.torusHomotopyEquiv.toFun (torusClass p q)) = 0) :
    q = 0 := by
  have hq : H1map h.openToTorus (H1map (puncturedToOpen f Φ)
      (H1map h.torusHomotopyEquiv.toFun (torusClass p q))) = torusClass 0 q := by
    rw [← H1map_comp, ← H1map_comp,
      show (h.openToTorus.comp (puncturedToOpen f Φ)).comp h.torusHomotopyEquiv.toFun =
        ⟨fun q ↦ (1, q.2), by fun_prop⟩ from ContinuousMap.ext h.openToTorus_puncturedToOpen,
      H1map_torusClass]
    exact congrArg _ (loopClass_eq_of_apply_eq _ _ fun t ↦ by simp)
  rw [hpq, map_zero, eq_comm, torusClass_eq_zero_iff] at hq
  exact hq.2

/-! ### The Mayer–Vietoris computation -/

variable [T2Space X]
  (h₁ : IsZero ((reducedSingularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) 1).obj (TopCat.of X)))
  (h₂ : IsZero ((reducedSingularHomologyFunctor (ModuleCat.of ℤ ℤ) 2).obj (TopCat.of X)))

/-- The inclusion of the boundary torus of the exterior in the knot complement. -/
private abbrev frontierToComplement (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    C(↥(frontier (Φ '' {p | ‖(p.1 : ℂ)‖ < 1})ᶜ), ↥(range f)ᶜ) :=
  ContinuousMap.inclusion h.frontier_subset_compl_range

/-- The radial expansion of the torus at radius `1 / 2` onto the boundary torus, inside the knot
complement. -/
private def expandHomotopy (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    ((puncturedToComplement f Φ).comp h.torusHomotopyEquiv.toFun).Homotopy
      (h.frontierToComplement.comp ⟨h.exteriorFrontierHomeomorph, by fun_prop⟩) where
  toFun x := ⟨Φ (radialPoint ((1 + x.1) / 2)
      ⟨by linarith [unitInterval.nonneg x.1], by linarith [unitInterval.le_one x.1]⟩ x.2),
    h.apply_radialPoint_notMem_range (by linarith [unitInterval.nonneg x.1]) _ _⟩
  continuous_toFun := (h.isEmbedding.continuous.comp (continuous_radialPoint (by fun_prop) _
    continuous_snd)).subtype_mk _
  map_zero_left q := Subtype.ext <| by
    simp only [ContinuousMap.comp_apply, ContinuousMap.inclusion_apply_coe,
      coe_torusHomotopyEquiv_apply]
    exact congrArg Φ (radialPoint_congr (by simp) _ _ q)
  map_one_left q := Subtype.ext <| by
    simp only [ContinuousMap.comp_apply, ContinuousMap.inclusion_apply_coe,
      ContinuousMap.coe_mk, coe_exteriorFrontierHomeomorph_apply]
    exact congrArg Φ ((radialPoint_congr (by norm_num) _ ⟨zero_le_one, le_rfl⟩ q).trans
      (radialPoint_one q _))

/-- The knot is closed. -/
private theorem isClosed_range_loop (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) : IsClosed (range f) := by
  rw [show f = fun z ↦ Φ (0, z) from funext fun z ↦ (h.apply_zero z).symm]
  exact (isCompact_range
    (h.isEmbedding.continuous.comp (continuous_const.prodMk continuous_id))).isClosed

include h₁ h₂ in
private theorem mayerVietoris (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    (∀ x, H1map (puncturedToOpen f Φ) x = 0 → H1map (puncturedToComplement f Φ) x = 0 →
      x = 0) ∧
    ∀ c, ∃ x, H1map (puncturedToOpen f Φ) x = 0 ∧ H1map (puncturedToComplement f Φ) x = c :=
  mayerVietoris_one (X := X) h.isOpen_image h.isClosed_range_loop.isOpen_compl
    (eq_univ_of_forall fun x ↦ (em (x ∈ range f)).imp (fun hx ↦ h.range_subset_image hx) id)
    h₁ h₂

include h₁ h₂ in
/-- Every class of the knot complement is a multiple of the meridian at radius `1 / 2`. -/
private theorem exists_zsmul_eq (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ)
    (c : ((singularChains ℤ).obj (TopCat.of ↥(range f)ᶜ)).homology 1) :
    ∃ k : ℤ, k • H1map (puncturedToComplement f Φ) (H1map h.torusHomotopyEquiv.toFun
      (torusClass 1 0)) = c := by
  obtain ⟨x, hxU, rfl⟩ := (h.mayerVietoris h₁ h₂).2 c
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := (bijective_H1map h.torusHomotopyEquiv).2 x
  obtain ⟨p, q, rfl⟩ := exists_eq_torusClass y
  obtain rfl := h.eq_zero_of_H1map_puncturedToOpen_eq_zero hxU
  refine ⟨p, ?_⟩
  rw [torusClass_eq p 0, zero_smul, add_zero, map_zsmul, map_zsmul]

include h₁ h₂ in
/-- The meridian at radius `1 / 2` has infinite order in the knot complement. -/
private theorem eq_zero_of_zsmul_eq_zero (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) {k : ℤ}
    (hk : k • H1map (puncturedToComplement f Φ) (H1map h.torusHomotopyEquiv.toFun
      (torusClass 1 0)) = 0) : k = 0 := by
  have hx := (h.mayerVietoris h₁ h₂).1 (H1map h.torusHomotopyEquiv.toFun (k • torusClass 1 0))
    (by rw [map_zsmul, map_zsmul, h.H1map_puncturedToOpen_torusClass_zero]; exact zsmul_zero k)
    (by rw [map_zsmul, map_zsmul, hk])
  rw [← map_zero (H1map h.torusHomotopyEquiv.toFun)] at hx
  have hk0 : torusClass k 0 = 0 := by
    rw [torusClass_eq, zero_smul, add_zero]
    exact (bijective_H1map h.torusHomotopyEquiv).1 hx
  exact ((torusClass_eq_zero_iff k 0).1 hk0).1

/-! ### The meridian generates the homology of the knot complement -/

/-- The map `H₁(T; ℤ) → H₁(X ∖ K; ℤ)` induced by the inclusion of the boundary torus `T` of the
exterior of the knot `K = range f` into the knot complement. -/
def boundaryHomologyMap (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    h.framedBoundaryTorus.H →ₗ[ℤ] ((singularChains ℤ).obj (TopCat.of ↥(range f)ᶜ)).homology 1 :=
  H1map h.frontierToComplement

/-- `TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.boundaryHomologyMap` is induced by the inclusion of the
boundary torus of the exterior into the knot complement. -/
theorem boundaryHomologyMap_def (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    h.boundaryHomologyMap = (HomologicalComplex.homologyMap ((singularChains ℤ).map
      (TopCat.ofHom (ContinuousMap.inclusion h.frontier_subset_compl_range))) 1).hom :=
  (rfl)

/-- On the boundary torus, the `(p, q)` curve is homologous in the knot complement to the
`(p, q)` curve at radius `1 / 2`. -/
private theorem boundaryHomologyMap_torusCurveClass (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ)
    (p q : ℤ) :
    h.boundaryHomologyMap (FramedBoundaryTorus.torusCurveClass h.exteriorFrontierHomeomorph p q) =
      H1map (puncturedToComplement f Φ) (H1map h.torusHomotopyEquiv.toFun (torusClass p q)) := by
  have hH := LinearMap.congr_fun (H1map_eq_of_homotopic ⟨h.expandHomotopy⟩) (torusClass p q)
  rw [H1map_comp, H1map_comp, H1map_torusClass ⟨h.exteriorFrontierHomeomorph, by fun_prop⟩,
    ← FramedBoundaryTorus.torusCurveClass_def] at hH
  exact hH.symm

/-- **The meridian generates the first homology of the knot complement.** For a knot with a solid
torus neighbourhood `Φ` in a Hausdorff space `X` with `H₁(X; ℤ) = H₂(X; ℤ) = 0`, the first
integral homology of the knot complement is infinite cyclic, freely generated by the meridian of
`Φ`: this isomorphism `H₁(X ∖ K; ℤ) ≃ ℤ` sends the meridian to `1`
(`TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.complementHomologyEquiv_meridian`). For a knot in `S³` it is
the linking number with the knot, oriented so that the meridian of `Φ` has linking number `1`. -/
def complementHomologyEquiv (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    ((singularChains ℤ).obj (TopCat.of ↥(range f)ᶜ)).homology 1 ≃ₗ[ℤ] ℤ :=
  have hμ : h.boundaryHomologyMap (h.framedBoundaryTorus.basis 0) =
      H1map (puncturedToComplement f Φ) (H1map h.torusHomotopyEquiv.toFun (torusClass 1 0)) := by
    rw [FramedBoundaryTorus.ofHomeomorph_basis_zero, h.boundaryHomologyMap_torusCurveClass]
  -- `LinearMap.toSpanSingleton` uses the `Module ℤ` action of the homology object, while the
  -- computations above use `zsmul`; the two agree by `Int.cast_smul_eq_zsmul`.
  (LinearEquiv.ofBijective (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton ℤ _
    (h.boundaryHomologyMap (h.framedBoundaryTorus.basis 0)))
    ⟨fun k k' hkk' ↦ sub_eq_zero.1 <| h.eq_zero_of_zsmul_eq_zero h₁ h₂ <| by
        have hk : k • h.boundaryHomologyMap (h.framedBoundaryTorus.basis 0) =
            k' • h.boundaryHomologyMap (h.framedBoundaryTorus.basis 0) := by
          rw [← Int.cast_smul_eq_zsmul ℤ k, ← Int.cast_smul_eq_zsmul ℤ k']
          exact hkk'
        rw [← hμ, sub_zsmul, hk, add_neg_cancel],
      fun c ↦ by
        obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := h.exists_zsmul_eq h₁ h₂ c
        refine ⟨k, ?_⟩
        rw [← hk, ← hμ, ← Int.cast_smul_eq_zsmul ℤ k]
        rfl⟩).symm

/-- The inverse of `TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.complementHomologyEquiv` sends `k` to `k`
times the meridian. -/
@[simp]
theorem complementHomologyEquiv_symm_apply (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) (k : ℤ) :
    (h.complementHomologyEquiv h₁ h₂).symm k =
      k • h.boundaryHomologyMap (h.framedBoundaryTorus.basis 0) :=
  Int.cast_smul_eq_zsmul ℤ k _

/-- The meridian goes to `1`. -/
@[simp]
theorem complementHomologyEquiv_meridian (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    h.complementHomologyEquiv h₁ h₂ (h.boundaryHomologyMap (h.framedBoundaryTorus.basis 0)) =
      1 := by
  have := (h.complementHomologyEquiv h₁ h₂).apply_symm_apply 1
  rwa [complementHomologyEquiv_symm_apply, one_zsmul] at this

/-- The **framing number** of the solid torus neighbourhood `Φ`: the longitude of `Φ` is
homologous in the knot complement to `framingNumber` times the meridian. Equivalently, the
longitude of `Φ` is `λ₀ + n · μ` for the preferred longitude `λ₀`
(`TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.preferredFramedBoundaryTorus_basis_one`). For a knot in `S³`
it is the linking number of the longitude of `Φ` with the knot. -/
def framingNumber (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) : ℤ :=
  h.complementHomologyEquiv h₁ h₂ (h.boundaryHomologyMap (h.framedBoundaryTorus.basis 1))

/-- A class of the boundary torus with `(μ, λ)`-coordinates `(p, q)` is homologous in the knot
complement to `p + n q` times the meridian, `n` the framing number. -/
theorem complementHomologyEquiv_boundaryHomologyMap (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ)
    (x : h.framedBoundaryTorus.H) :
    h.complementHomologyEquiv h₁ h₂ (h.boundaryHomologyMap x) =
      (h.framedBoundaryTorus.coord x).1 +
        h.framingNumber h₁ h₂ * (h.framedBoundaryTorus.coord x).2 := by
  conv_lhs => rw [← h.framedBoundaryTorus.coord.symm_apply_apply x,
    FramedBoundaryTorus.coord_symm_apply]
  rw [map_add, map_zsmul, map_zsmul, map_add, map_zsmul, map_zsmul,
    complementHomologyEquiv_meridian, ← framingNumber, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul, mul_one,
    mul_comm]

/-- A class of the boundary torus with `(μ, λ)`-coordinates `(p, q)` is null-homologous in the
knot complement exactly when `p + n q = 0`, `n` the framing number. -/
theorem boundaryHomologyMap_eq_zero_iff (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ)
    (x : h.framedBoundaryTorus.H) :
    h.boundaryHomologyMap x = 0 ↔
      (h.framedBoundaryTorus.coord x).1 +
        h.framingNumber h₁ h₂ * (h.framedBoundaryTorus.coord x).2 = 0 := by
  rw [← complementHomologyEquiv_boundaryHomologyMap h₁ h₂, LinearEquiv.map_eq_zero_iff]

/-! ### The preferred framing -/

/-- The **preferred framing** of the boundary torus of the exterior: the meridian `μ` of `Φ`
together with the **preferred longitude** `λ₀ = λ - n · μ`, `n` the framing number of `Φ`. The
preferred longitude is null-homologous in the knot complement
(`TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.boundaryHomologyMap_preferredFramedBoundaryTorus_basis_one`)
and generates the kernel of `H₁(T) → H₁(X ∖ K)`
(`TauCeti.IsSolidTorusNeighborhood.ker_boundaryHomologyMap`), so up to sign it is the only
longitude completing `μ` to a basis that is null-homologous in the knot complement. For a knot in
`S³` this is the Seifert framing of surgery theory.

This is reducible so that its torus is the boundary torus of the exterior for consumers, and hence
that classes of `h.framedBoundaryTorus.H` are classes of its homology. -/
abbrev preferredFramedBoundaryTorus (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) : FramedBoundaryTorus :=
  h.framedBoundaryTorus.shiftLongitude (-h.framingNumber h₁ h₂)

/-- The preferred framing keeps the meridian of `Φ`. -/
theorem preferredFramedBoundaryTorus_basis_zero (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    (h.preferredFramedBoundaryTorus h₁ h₂).basis 0 = h.framedBoundaryTorus.basis 0 :=
  FramedBoundaryTorus.shiftLongitude_basis_zero _ _

/-- The preferred longitude is `λ - n · μ`, for the longitude `λ` and meridian `μ` of `Φ` and its
framing number `n`. -/
theorem preferredFramedBoundaryTorus_basis_one (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    (h.preferredFramedBoundaryTorus h₁ h₂).basis 1 =
      h.framedBoundaryTorus.basis 1 - h.framingNumber h₁ h₂ • h.framedBoundaryTorus.basis 0 := by
  rw [FramedBoundaryTorus.shiftLongitude_basis_one, neg_zsmul, sub_eq_add_neg]

/-- **In the preferred framing a class goes to its meridian coordinate.** A class of the boundary
torus is homologous in the knot complement to its `μ`-coordinate in the preferred framing times
the meridian. -/
theorem complementHomologyEquiv_boundaryHomologyMap_preferred (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ)
    (x : h.framedBoundaryTorus.H) :
    h.complementHomologyEquiv h₁ h₂ (h.boundaryHomologyMap x) =
      ((h.preferredFramedBoundaryTorus h₁ h₂).coord x).1 := by
  rw [complementHomologyEquiv_boundaryHomologyMap, FramedBoundaryTorus.coord_shiftLongitude]
  ring

/-- **The preferred longitude is null-homologous in the knot complement.** -/
@[simp]
theorem boundaryHomologyMap_preferredFramedBoundaryTorus_basis_one
    (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    h.boundaryHomologyMap ((h.preferredFramedBoundaryTorus h₁ h₂).basis 1) = 0 := by
  rw [← (h.complementHomologyEquiv h₁ h₂).map_eq_zero_iff,
    complementHomologyEquiv_boundaryHomologyMap_preferred, FramedBoundaryTorus.coord_basis_one]

/-- **The preferred longitude generates the classes of the boundary torus that are
null-homologous in the knot complement.** -/
theorem ker_boundaryHomologyMap (h : IsSolidTorusNeighborhood f Φ) :
    LinearMap.ker h.boundaryHomologyMap =
      Submodule.span ℤ {(h.preferredFramedBoundaryTorus h₁ h₂).basis 1} := by
  set T := h.preferredFramedBoundaryTorus h₁ h₂
  ext x
  rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, ← (h.complementHomologyEquiv h₁ h₂).map_eq_zero_iff,
    complementHomologyEquiv_boundaryHomologyMap_preferred, Submodule.mem_span_singleton]
  constructor
  · intro hx
    refine ⟨(T.coord x).2, T.coord.injective ?_⟩
    rw [LinearEquiv.map_smul, FramedBoundaryTorus.coord_basis_one]
    exact Prod.ext (by rw [Prod.smul_fst, smul_zero]; exact hx.symm) (by simp)
  · rintro ⟨k, rfl⟩
    rw [LinearEquiv.map_smul, FramedBoundaryTorus.coord_basis_one]
    simp

end IsSolidTorusNeighborhood

end TauCeti
